      "message": "I was thinking that the SkSharedContext would keep track of the lifetime of the below pointers using an sk_sp\n* fExecutor\n* fLogHandler\n* fEventTracer\n\nSince these are meant to be accessed by multiple SkContexts. Using sk_sp would also allow SkContextOptions to be copyable and thus be able to be passed into the context factory functions.\n\nI was going to implement the logic to add the sk_ref_cnt for SkExecutor and SkEventTracer in a follow up cl, but I added it here for simplicity. Let me know if there is any reason SkExecutor or SkEventTracer should not be ref_cnted\n\nfImageGeneratorFactory and fSVGDecoderFactory are function pointers for factories, so they don\u0027t require any ownership\n\n\nHere is the link to the specific part of the design doc this covers\n* https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wtwgf-Bn9XA_P6DZiboeC7NgqreBxaxFWd36tD2Wzdo/edit?tab\u003dt.4rsc8withiat#heading\u003dh.ok8yo3sjpj7i",
